--- Error line tracking
--- Every error-value carries the source line where the error originated

--- int parse error
x = int['hello']
log['int error ok: `x.ok`']
log['int error reason: `x.reason`']
log['int error kind: `x.kind`']

--- file read error
content = read['nonexistent_file.txt']
log['read error ok: `content.ok`']
log['read error reason: `content.reason`']
log['read error kind: `content.kind`']

--- successful values have line 0
y = int['42']
log['ok ok: `y.ok`']
log['ok kind: `y.kind`']

--- raw values also have line 0
z = 5
log['raw kind: `z.kind`']
